# ==============================================================================
# Git Ignore Configuration for Amiga 500 Emulator
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. Environment & Local Host Configuration
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local environment variables (e.g. RAG_CACHE_FILE path, Qdrant URL, host ports).
# Critical for tools and scripts; preserved across worktrees via copy.
.env

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 3. Editor & Workspace UI State (Safe to delete)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local Obsidian vault state: active workspace tabs and remembered cursor positions.
Obsidian/Amiga/.obsidian/workspace.json
Obsidian/Amiga/.obsidian/plugins/remember-cursor-position/cursor-positions.json

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 4. Python Runtime Bytecode Cache (Safe to delete)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ephemeral compiled bytecode created when running repository tools (*.py).
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Local agent execution plans, diagnostics, and previous tool installations.
.agent/tasks/
.agent/tmp/
.agent/tools/
# Bootstrap-provisioned M68000 assembler binaries and license.
/tools/m68k-asm/
# Legacy generated SingleStep reports; current runs use .agent/tmp/singlestep.
/tests/singlestep/
# Legacy generated benchmark reports; tracked baselines and traces remain visible.
/tests/benchmarks/quick/
/tests/benchmarks/standard/
/tests/benchmarks/thorough/
# Local CPU performance test runs; approved baselines remain tracked.
/benchmarks/results/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 5. Rust Cargo Build Outputs (Safe to delete / Regenerated on build)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Target compilation directory for Rust crates. Kept isolated per worktree to
# prevent concurrent Cargo compiler locks.
target/

# ==============================================================================
# 7. PRESERVED EXTERNAL ASSETS & REFERENCE DATA (CRITICAL - DO NOT PURGE / DELETE!)
# ==============================================================================
# The items below are excluded from Git history to avoid committing multi-gigabyte
# external binaries, but THEY CONTAIN CRITICAL DATA AND MUST NEVER BE DELETED.
#
# They are physically copied into isolated Git worktrees by `tools/worktree.ps1`:
# ==============================================================================

# Physical 68000 silicon test vectors (SingleStepTests, 6.5 GB) & clean-room
# reference emulators (vAmiga, Musashi, MAME, WinUAE).
/ref_src/

# Ingested Commodore hardware manuals and technical specifications
# (Explicitly ignored per item to ensure visibility of any new or untracked files):
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/68000 Programmer's Reference Manual*/
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/68000 User's Manual*/
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/A500 A2000 Technical Reference Manual*/
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/Hardware Reference Manual*/
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/Instruction Prefetch on the Motorola 68000 Processor*
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/Undocumented features of OCS, ECS and AGA chipsets*
Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/Motorola 68000 DIVU & DIVS Cycle-Accurate Timing Analysis-*.md
/Obsidian/Amiga/Reference/.cache/

# Graphify AST knowledge graph database, semantic indices, and architecture maps.
# Physically copied as a seed for new worktrees, then refreshed locally with graphify update.
/graphify-out/

# Keir Fraser Amiga Test Kit floppy disk images (.adf), debug symbols, and release docs.
/tools/AmigaTestKit*/

# not worthy roadmap.md and git history itself
TODO.md
